87
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:27,800
You're her friend.

88
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:29,200
Do you know what's up with her?

89
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:29,940
No.

90
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,060
No one was home when I went by there.

91
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,180
Where is she?

92
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,160
I mean, if she was sick, we would've heard.

93
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:35,920
Yeah.

94
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:38,740
But there's been no word yet from her mom, anyway.

95
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:49,580
Come on, I'm sure she'll show up sooner or later like she always does.

96
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:51,220
So how about we get started?

97
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,160
Really?

98
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,920
No one was there this morning either, huh?

99
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,280
Are you worried?

100
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:00,480
Mm-hmm.

101
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:03,180
You don't look like you're all that worried.

102
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,320
I'm just trying to stay calm.

103
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:08,520
Like you always say, panicking never helps anyone.

104
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,880
You're right.

105
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:14,000
I tried calling Kaio's yesterday and today, but there's no answer.

106
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:17,460
Also, I tried calling the place where her mother works.

107
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:19,080
They told me she hasn't been in.

108
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,360
Well then, call the CPS people or the police!

109
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:24,440
The police, huh?

110
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:25,860
I don't know.

111
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,200
I'd hate to open a can of worms.

112
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,660
For someone else, that is.

113
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:35,680
I called CPS yesterday, though.

114
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,300
They'll visit her house today.

115
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:39,380
And I'm going to meet them.

116
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,980
I'm pretty sure if we all show up there, we'll get to the bottom of things.

117
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:47,220
It's like I always say in class, where there's a will, there's a way.

118
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,380
You're the best!

119
00:06:49,380 --> 00:07:02,620
Miss Inazuki, we're with Child Protective Services.

120
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:06,940
Is she even home?

121
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:10,280
Well, all the lights are on, so someone has to be.

122
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,360
Why don't we have a look around the back?

123
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,500
Miss Inazuki, are you home?

124
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:18,620
Kaio?

125
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:23,780
I'm coming in.

126
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:24,260
What?

127
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:25,920
You can't just walk in.

128
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:26,540
Don't worry.

129
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,640
If anyone complains, I'll take the blame.

130
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:32,060
The girl's been missing for three days now.

131
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,100
It's worth a shot.

132
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:45,720
The stove and the lights are on.

133
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,180
There's a half-eaten dinner on the coffee table.

134
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,000
I don't see Kaio's coat anywhere.

135
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,920
By the looks of it, her mom was just here a minute ago.

136
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,160
She left in a hurry.

137
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,040
I bet she saw us pull up.

138
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,640
By the time we got to the door, she was out the back.

139
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:02,600
Damn it.

140
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,480
I was hoping we could take custody of the girl tonight.

141
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,820
Look, her mother can't stay out in this cold all night.

142
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:11,220
As soon as we leave, I'm sure she'll come back.

143
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,820
We can try again tomorrow morning.

144
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,480
I'm worried about Kaio's safety, though.

145
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,840
We could get the police to put an APB out on the mom.

146
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:19,740
Uh-uh.

147
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:22,020
I have a feeling Kaio's safe.

148
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,540
In fact, I'm positive she is.

149
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,820
Okay, we'll take your word for it.

150
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:27,940
We'll leave for now.

151
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,100
Give the mother a chance to calm down.

152
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:35,580
Mr. Yashiro and Child Protective Services were just at your house.

153
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,700
They were looking for your mom, but she wasn't there.

154
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:41,500
By tomorrow, all of this might be over.

155
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:45,260
Kaio, they said they'd take you away from her.

156
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,560
That's okay.

157
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,580
I'd be way happier without her.

158
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,840
We knew if they took her away from her mom,

159
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:54,040
they'd be taking her away from us, too.

160
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:57,780
It'll be hard to go, but I'll be fine.

161
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:01,960
Whenever I think of you guys, I'll remember all the fun we had.

162
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:07,900
Satoru, I know it's a little late, but...

163
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,560
I finished your birthday present.

164
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,320
Here you go.

165
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:16,320
I'll give you your present tomorrow.

166
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:17,540
Promise.

167
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,220
Thank you.

168
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:34,540
It feels like...

169
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:35,180
I don't know.

170
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,240
Like I've been waiting for this forever.

171
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:44,440
It doesn't take much to make you tear up, huh?

172
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:45,880
Wait, what?

173
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:49,120
Oh, hey, Satoru.

174
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,600
Can you spend the night?

175
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,560
That's totally gutsy!

176
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:54,560
Dorks.

177
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,360
Last night, someone came in while I was sleeping.

178
00:09:58,260 --> 00:09:59,400
He just walked in.

179
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,540
I don't think he knew I was here.

180
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,700
But it scared me.

181
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:07,280
Maybe it was a security guard or a janitor.

182
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,020
It could have been anyone.

183
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,980
Some pervy kid stashing his porn.

184
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:13,000
Who knows?

185
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:14,720
It was a grown-up.

186
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,840
Whoever it was was mad.

187
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,660
He kicked that box super hard.

188
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:20,780
Let's open it.

189
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,940
I hope it's nothing worse than porn.

190
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,900
What's that for?

191
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:41,720
I knew.

192
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:44,980
I knew right away what all that stuff was for.

193
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,580
Then it hit me.

194
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:51,080
This old bus we were in was out behind Izumi Elementary.

195
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:55,760
The school where Aya Nakanishi, the killer's next victim, went.

196
00:10:55,760 --> 00:11:02,100
We hadn't escaped the loop of kidnappings and murders yet.

197
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:10,880
March the 2nd.

198
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:16,400
Sometime after 10 that night, Kaio disappeared from the shed behind her house.

199
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:20,940
Tracks found around the shed were from a pair of rubber boots.

200
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,260
They matched a pair Yuki owned.

201
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:30,580
The killer put Kaio in a walk-in freezer and sprayed water on her to make her freeze to death faster.

202
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:36,000
Then, the killer took her body back to the shed before dawn.

203
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,400
We can't stay here.

204
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:46,460
This bus is at the center of the killer's routine.

205
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:51,720
It's not safe here.

206
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:53,260
No.

207
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:54,400
No, it's not.

208
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:57,380
Our plan was to have someone find Kaio here.

209
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:01,380
But now, after seeing this crap, we better move her.

210
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:02,600
Mm-hmm.

211
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,640
We don't want some creep to find her.

212
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,160
Well, I hope you have a plan B.

213
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,460
I do.

214
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:11,580
Awesome.

215
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:12,480
Okay.

216
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:13,660
Let's clear out.

217
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,820
Remember what that footprint looks like.

218
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:27,540
What's all that black stuff?

219
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,560
Charcoal on a stove.

220
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,460
Was the killer going to use this to...

221
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:43,320
No!

222
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:44,140
No!

223
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:45,940
Satoru.

224
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:47,900
Flipping out isn't going to help.

225
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:50,480
Yeah, you're right.

226
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,440
I gotta keep a clear head.

227
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:56,980
All right.

228
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,120
Let's get going.

229
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,980
It was such a cool hideout.

230
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:00,780
Right.

231
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,840
But not of some weirdos using it, too.

232
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:03,520
Yeah.

233
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:05,740
However we do it,

234
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:09,380
we need to make damn sure Kaio stays out of the killer's range.

235
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:13,280
But now, with Child Protective Services on the case,

236
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:15,260
the future has to change.

237
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,540
It's got to.

238
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:21,720
Wait.

239
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:23,580
This is plan B?

240
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:24,520
Mm-hmm.

241
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:25,800
Simple, huh?

242
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,740
There's just one last hurdle.

243
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:30,680
It would have saved us a lot of hassle if you thought of...

244
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,360
I'm home.

245
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:34,140
It's about time.

246
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:38,140
Um...

247
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:38,780
Um...

248
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:39,440
Uh...

249
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:39,940
Hello.

250
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:40,980
Hello.

251
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,280
All right.

252
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:44,520
What's going on?

253
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,440
I'm helping a friend in trouble.

254
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:52,320
That's what.

255
00:13:52,320 --> 00:14:03,880
Way to go, guys.

256
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:04,720
Good job.

257
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,740
I was hoping you'd be okay with this.

258
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:10,320
For a sec, I thought you were gonna kick my butt.

259
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,200
I did it again.

260
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,860
Now, why on earth would you think that?

261
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:17,100
This is exactly what friends are for.

262
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:21,840
What you cooking?

263
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,140
I could smell it when I came in.

264
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,400
Oh, nothing much.

265
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:27,240
Just a big fat pot of curry is all.

266
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,300
I had a feeling you'd be bringing over a couple of friends tonight.

267
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:32,480
My mom can read me like a book.

268
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,520
Don't just stand there.

269
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:35,380
Pull up a chair.

270
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,680
Would you like some curry?

271
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,340
Yes, please.

272
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:39,420
It smells yummy.

273
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:44,220
It's good I brought everyone, because you made a ton.

274
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,820
If you didn't, you'd be eating curry for the rest of the month.

275
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,160
Um, Miss Fujinuma?

276
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,120
I brought this back.

277
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:55,540
It was delicious.

278
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,840
Well, my job's done for the night.

279
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,400
Have fun washing the dishes, kiddo.

280
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:05,680
Thanks, Mom.

281
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,260
See you later.

282
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:07,960
Bye-bye.

283
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,040
Later, guys.

284
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:14,820
Mr. Yashiro, this is Satoru Fujinuma's mom.

285
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:17,800
Actually, I do.

286
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:20,900
Satoru just brought Kayo back to my place, and she's okay.

287
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,360
Ah, what a relief.

288
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,440
That's good to hear.

289
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,240
I knew they were in this together.

290
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:29,880
Yeah, it's great, but what happens to her now?

291
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:31,980
Will she be put in foster care?

292
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:34,000
Good question.

293
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:37,080
You know, I've been thinking about it, and I might have an idea.

294
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:41,720
No, we tried to, but her mother wasn't home.

295
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:45,620
Maybe you can help, but only if you don't mind.

296
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:55,000
Hey, Kayo, you want to spend the night?

297
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:55,920
Mm-hmm.

298
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:55,940
Mm-hmm.

299
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:00,460
Hello?

300
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,460
I'm sorry to call so late.

301
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:05,960
I'm Gaku Yashiro, a teacher at Mikoto Elementary.

302
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:08,700
I need to talk to you about Kayo.

303
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:11,280
He's called Wonder Guy.

304
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,200
Isn't he cool?

305
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:15,540
Okay, guys, bath time.

306
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,860
Who wants to go first?

307
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:18,960
I'll go after you.

308
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,540
You know what?

309
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:23,680
How about we go together?

310
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:33,080
Hey, Kayo, come here and let me wash your hair.

311
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:35,640
Um, no thank you.

312
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:36,260
I can do it.

313
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:36,840
It's okay.

314
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:37,880
I want to.

315
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,740
How are we doing, miss?

316
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,540
Are we feeling fabulous yet?

317
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:48,260
And now it's time for...

318
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,560
Tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle.

319
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,560
And more tickles.

320
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:58,700
And more, and more.

321
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:02,540
Hello, you're 29.

322
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:09,140
We better dry your hair or you're going to catch a cold.

323
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:18,240
Um, you guys like to have a good bath?

324
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:19,300
Yeah.

325
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,620
It was lots of fun.

326
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:23,760
That's good.

327
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,480
Wait, those are your pajamas?

328
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,900
Now they are.

329
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:28,840
I bought them for her.

330
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:29,940
Witch.

331
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:33,220
These are fresh and ready to go.

332
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,380
They're super soft.

333
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,280
Thank you.

334
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,600
Have you done this before?

335
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:39,520
You gotta pull your end tight.

336
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,780
This totally reminds me.

337
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,200
The class took a trip to Hakodate

338
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,900
and the view from the top of the mountain was rad.

339
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:47,580
What?

340
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,320
You've never been to Hakodate.

341
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:50,340
Crap.

342
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,140
Oh, must have been a photo I saw.

343
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:54,840
Okay.

344
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:57,060
You ready for lights out?

345
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:57,940
Yes.

346
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,040
Oh, it's so funny.

347
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:04,160
My house doesn't have a night light.

348
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,140
Oh, yeah?

349
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,900
I can turn it off if you want.

350
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:07,840
Uh-uh.

351
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,300
It's fine like this.

352
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:11,260
Why don't we leave it on tonight?

353
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:13,320
You got it.

354
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:14,900
Thanks, Satoru.

355
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:17,940
Night, guys.

356
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,040
Night, Mom.

357
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:33,580
I'm not in the way here, am I?

358
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:34,160
Yep.

359
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,400
No, of course not.

360
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,380
There I go again.

361
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:38,500
Stop.

362
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:38,680
Stop.

363
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,580
What'd you do that for?

364
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:41,980
Oops.

365
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,020
I meant to do this.

366
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:43,380
Ow.

367
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,340
And this.

368
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:45,020
Stop it.

369
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:45,540
Never.

370
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,820
You're an idiot.

371
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,260
Good morning.

372
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:07,300
Morning.

373
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:10,900
You awake?

374
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,220
If you are, shake a leg.

375
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,800
Breakfast is going to get cold.

376
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:16,580
Okay.

377
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,180
I'm starving.

378
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:28,240
Wait.

379
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,160
No curry?

380
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,500
That's your dinner.

381
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,080
For the next month.

382
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:32,600
What?

383
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:34,760
There can't be that much left.

384
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:37,240
You'll just have to invite everyone over again.

385
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:43,180
Bye-bye.

386
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:48,580
Oh.

387
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:04,980
Oh.

388
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:09,940
Missou –

389
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:39,460
Mm-hmm.

390
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:56,880
Goddamn little!

391
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:00,980
Mom?

392
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:11,440
Kaio! You little shit! Where the hell have you been?

393
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,360
I'll shoot!

394
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,720
I should have known.

395
00:21:34,980 --> 00:21:39,320
Kunaishivi mo…yorokobi mo…

396
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:43,820
Subbete…

397
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:47,800
Bona inaru p eating Canada

398
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,160
Yasaishiku naaru…

399
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:54,780
ことだと figurabisa no subete…

400
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:58,000
Undo na ni naru…

401
00:21:58,080 --> 00:22:02,020
protecting

402
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:32,000
See you next time.

403
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:46,020
君が笑うこの世界の歌 乗り戻すよ

